course: dictionary
lesson: 13970
title: A word that goes on and on
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A litany is a long prayer or a long list. In church, the leader says a line, the people answer with the same words, and this goes on for a long time. «The priest led the litany, and the people answered, "Lord, have mercy."» The clue is the repeating: the same answer again and again.
explain: Outside church, a litany is a long list, often of complaints or problems. «Mum read out a litany of complaints: the bus was late, the soup was cold and the dog had eaten her shoe.» The list seems to go on and on, so you know it is long, and the words keep repeating in the same way.
explain: When you meet litany, ask two questions. Is it long? Is it repeated? If the answer is yes to both, you have found the meaning. Then try it in the sentence: a litany of complaints means a long list of complaints.
fact: A litany is a long prayer where a leader says a line and the people answer.
fact: A litany can also be a long list of things, often complaints or problems, that seems to go on and on.
fact: Church litanies are found in Catholic, Anglican and Orthodox services.
fact: «A litany of mistakes» means a long list of mistakes.
fact: The word litany tells the reader that something is long and repeated.
exercise: «The priest led the litany, and the people answered each line.» What is a litany in this sentence? | A short song for one voice | *A long prayer where a leader and the people take turns | A map of the church | A kind of cake baked in church
exercise: Which word means a long list of complaints or problems that seems to go on and on? | *litany | ancient | famished | glum
exercise: «Mum groaned at the litany of complaints about the soggy chips.» What does the word litany tell the reader? | It is a happy surprise | It is short and sweet | It means a wet, grey day | *It is long and repeated
test: «The teacher gave a litany of rules: no running, no talking, no chewing gum, no late homework.» What does litany mean here? | A short hug | *A long list that goes on and on | A kind of bread | A quiet whisper
test: In church, a litany is a prayer where the people answer the leader. Which answer shows this? | "Ouch, that hurt!" | "The bus is late" | "Let us sing a quiet song in the garden" | *"Lord, have mercy," said everyone, again and again
exam: What is a litany? | A short, quiet word spoken once | *A long prayer or a long, repeated list | A grey and wet day in Scotland | A type of petrol station
